<title>FRANCE: French crude imports, margins rose in November 199.</title>
<headline>French crude imports, margins rose in November 199.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's industry ministry on Thursday issued the following data for deliveries to refineries.</p>
<p>Crude deliveries are by origin ('000 tonnes). Total includes modest deliveries from domestic French crude production.</p>
<p>					  Nov 1996   Oct 1996   Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Total				 7,500	7,387	6,556</p>
<p>    including Saudi Arabia	  1,771	1,442	1,318</p>
<p>		  Iraq			  0	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Iran			724	  483	  833</p>
<p>		  Kuwait			7	    0	   10</p>
<p>		  Algeria		   279	  313	  272</p>
<p>		  Libya		     244	   80	   78</p>
<p>		  Nigeria		   724	  713	  390</p>
<p>		  Britain		   768	1,547	  653</p>
<p>		  Norway		  1,813	1,228	1,663</p>
<p>		  ex-USSR		   579	  859	  665</p>
<p>The ministry also released the following data for French refining margins, based on North Sea Brent crude ($/barrel).</p>
<p>			    Nov 1996  Oct 1996  Sep 1996  Nov 1995</p>
<p>    Refining Margin     3.36	2.84	2.65	2.30</p>
<p>French plants ran at 99 percent of capacity in November, up from 96 percent in October and 90 percent in November 1995.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
